# The bits a tutorial note's mode can carry beyond its low byte (see tutwin.c): a bit in the second byte holds the note (the flag at
# 0x8cc244 is set while it is up, and the button that answers it sets the flag at 0x8cc248), a bit in the high half is kept in the
# object and the answer adds it to the word at 0x9a64bc. Each is opened, shown and answered with Continue, then with End Tour.
25 load
26 state tw_fields 0x8cc1e4 0x5c
26 state tw_flags 0x8cc244 8
26 state tw_button 0x8cc224 8
26 state tw_ans 0x9a64b8 8
44 open tut_terrain_held
50 snap held
52 click 172 736          # Continue
56 snap held-continue
58 open tut_terrain_bits
64 snap bits
66 click 172 736
70 snap bits-continue
72 open tut_terrain_both
78 snap both
80 click 475 736          # End Tour
84 snap both-end
86 open tut_terrain_held
92 snap held-again
94 click 475 736
98 snap held-end
100 open tut_terrain_held0
106 snap held0
108 click 324 736          # Close: a positive id
112 snap held0-close
114 open tut_terrain_bits0
120 snap bits0
122 click 324 736
126 snap bits0-close
128 open tut_terrain_both0
134 snap both0
136 click 324 736
140 snap both0-close
142 close
